# Copy to .env and fill in what you need.
#
# With none of these set the site still runs and the form still works: it reads
# a brand's catalogue and produces a brief, and tells the brand a person will
# take it from there. What these turn on is the automatic path, where a brand
# fills the form and their experience builds and publishes with nobody touching
# it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- automation

# A GitHub token that may fire a repository_dispatch at EQUIPO-DEANNA/brand-factory.
# This is the switch. Without it, every submission waits for a human; with it,
# submitting the form starts a real build.
#
# Make it a fine-grained personal access token scoped to brand-factory ALONE.
# It needs exactly two repository permissions:
#
#   Contents:  Read and write   — firing the dispatch, and reading the build
#                                 markers and deployment records
#   Metadata:  Read             — granted automatically with Contents
#
# Deliberately NOT Actions:read. An earlier version counted the daily cap from
# the Actions API, which needs it — and the organisation's approval flow errors
# and drops the request, so it could not be granted at all. Everything is now
# counted from files the run writes into the repository, which Contents already
# covers. One fewer permission to beg for.
#
# Nothing wider than brand-factory: this token lives in a public-facing web app,
# and the blast radius of a leak should be one repo.
# GITHUB_FACTORY_TOKEN=

# Builds we are willing to start in a day without anyone looking. Each one costs
# real money at the image provider, and the form is open to anyone who can load
# the page, so this is the ceiling on what a bad afternoon can cost. Submissions
# past it are not lost; they are handed to a person.
# Default 12.
# MAX_BUILDS_PER_DAY=12

# ------------------------------------------------------------- notifications

# Any endpoint that accepts JSON — a Slack incoming webhook, Make, n8n. Gets the
# WHOLE brief for every submission, not a summary, because the brief is the only
# artefact a submission produces and we deliberately store it nowhere else.
# Failing to reach it never fails a submission.
# INTAKE_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- tuning

# How long /api/analyse may spend reading a shop's catalogue before it answers
# with a partial read. Keep it comfortably under the platform's function
# timeout: a killed function returns a blank 504, which tells the brand nothing.
# Default 45000.
# ANALYSE_BUDGET_MS=45000
